            'Attention: Query-Key-Value mechanism (Attention(Q,K,V) = softmax(QK^T / sqrt(d_k)) V), scaled dot-product prevents softmax saturation in high dimensions (dividing by sqrt(d_k) keeps variance of dot product ~1), attention weights form probability distribution over values, each value weighted by relevance to query, masks (causal mask: -inf in upper triangle for autoregressive, padding mask: -inf at padding positions to ignore them)',
            'Self-attention: all positions attend to all others (encoder bidirectional), causal self-attention (decoder — each position can only attend to itself and previous positions via triangular mask), cross-attention (decoder queries attend to encoder key/value outputs — necessary for seq2seq like T5), relative position bias (T5 with bias added to attention logits before softmax)',
            'Multi-head attention: h parallel attention heads, each head operates on projected Q/K/V with dimension d_k = d_model / h, heads capture different relationship types (syntax, semantics, positional), outputs concatenated and projected with W_O, allows model to attend to information from different representation subspaces at different positions simultaneously',
            'Positional encoding: sinusoidal (original Transformer — PE(pos,2i) = sin(pos/10000^(2i/d_model)), PE(pos,2i+1) = cos(...), relative position capture via sinusoidal periodicity, no learned parameters, extrapolates to unseen lengths), RoPE (Rotary Position Embedding — Llama, GPT-NeoX: apply rotation matrix to queries and keys based on position, preserves relative position useful for length generalization), ALiBi (linear bias based on position difference — used in BLOOM, MPT, simpler than RoPE, good length extrapolation)',
